      "findings": [
        "Both bases already use get_sync and the inproc synchronization cache; preserve upstream ownership/access checks rather than introducing parallel per-object hooks.",
        "Upstream server inproc_sync.c uses designated object_ops initializers. Rebase the macOS backend against this layout; do not copy the older positional initializer.",
        "CX transports a shared-memory index in get_inproc_sync_fd replies while upstream only transports an fd. Server protocol, client receive/close paths and generated tables must change together; no literal CX protocol version transplant.",
        "CX msync_wait_objs takes BOOLEAN wait_any; upstream linux_wait_objs takes WAIT_TYPE. Preserve WaitAny/WaitAll/WaitAll-one-object and APC status semantics explicitly.",
        "Highball0005 yield requires the actual msync backend and matching server fallback; the yield-only patch is not an implementation of macOS inproc synchronization."
      ]
    },
